RCV Vote Counter - 1
Hey, you're about to build something fun and intelligent — a voting simulator that mimics real-world elections! Using Ranked Choice Voting (RCV), your program will determine the winner based on how voters rank their preferences. This project strengthens your logic-building and prepares you for a web-based extension in Project 2.

What is RCV? In Ranked Choice Voting, each voter ranks candidates (1st, 2nd, 3rd...). We start by counting only the first-choice votes. If no candidate gets more than 50%, the one with the fewest votes is eliminated, and their votes are redistributed to the next choice. This continues until someone gets a majority or no one is left.

